# Serve the self-hosted CineX AltStore source from your EXISTING Caddy.
# gen-source.py writes deploy/ios-sideload/web/{apps.json,icon.png,CineX.ipa}.
# Point Caddy at that dir with ONE of the blocks below, then set SOURCE_BASE_URL to
# match the address the PHONE will use, and (re)run gen-source.py so the URLs in
# apps.json line up. Reload Caddy: `caddy reload` (or `systemctl reload caddy`).

# ---- Option A: dedicated LAN port (simplest; phone must be on the LAN) ----
# SOURCE_BASE_URL=http://192.168.10.128:8843
:8843 {
	root * /path/to/NuvioMobile/deploy/ios-sideload/web
	file_server
}

# ---- Option B: path under an existing site (reuses your TLS/domain) ----
# SOURCE_BASE_URL=https://hamrocinema.regmig.com/cinex-ios
# Add INSIDE your existing `hamrocinema.regmig.com { ... }` block:
#	handle_path /cinex-ios/* {
#		root * /path/to/NuvioMobile/deploy/ios-sideload/web
#		file_server
#	}

# ---- Option C: dedicated subdomain (clean https URL for the source) ----
# SOURCE_BASE_URL=https://ios.hamrocinema.regmig.com
# ios.hamrocinema.regmig.com {
#	root * /path/to/NuvioMobile/deploy/ios-sideload/web
#	file_server
# }

# Notes:
# - AltStore accepts plain http sources on a LAN; https (B/C) is nicer and works anywhere.
# - The .ipa is ~50-190 MB — make sure any upstream body/size limits allow it.
# - After every new CI build: re-run bootstrap.sh (pulls new .ipa + regenerates web/);
#   AltStore then offers the update OTA. No Caddy change needed on updates.
